(7432451, 1174090, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Oh, Marcel, I am afraid that this is a little bit of a misstep.  Technically it''s quite a good image, well lit, with well-defined rubber bands (though some in the bottom third or so are getting soft), but it''s simply too literal, and at this stage in his career, Bowie was not literal in his lyrics. The multitude of bands leads the eye all over the place, it needs to stop and settle somewhere. It may have been a better idea to read the lyrics and try to illustrate a line from the song, or if really stuck, go with a better known song.<br/> <br/>I did say that this was a misstep but you''re definitely on a journey!  Keep up the good work and keep on entering.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Oh, Marcel, I am afraid that this is a little bit of a misstep.  Technically it''s quite a good image, well lit, with well-defined rubber bands (though some in the bottom third or so are getting soft), but it''s simply too literal, and at this stage in his career, Bowie was not literal in his lyrics. The multitude of bands leads the eye all over the place, it needs to stop and settle somewhere. It may have been a better idea to read the lyrics and try to illustrate a line from the song, or if really stuck, go with a better known song. I did say that this was a misstep but you''re definitely on a journey!  Keep up the good work and keep on entering. Susan', '2016-01-27 18:24:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7432452, 1173906, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Hmm...the dog looks more like a cat than a dog, and I have my doubts as to whether you could get this shot with a 500mm f.4 unless you''re about 10 feet tall, and even then you would still barely squeeze the head in.  Part of it, maybe.  The effects, added or in-camera, are a little distracting and it seems that you have some odd material for floors in Russia.<br/> <br/>Still, you got some love from the more seditious members here - <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=74588" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">cutout</a> and <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=50695" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">posthumous</a> like it, so it can''t be all bad.  Getting a Posty is a bit of a compliment so make sure you post it prominently on your user page!<br/> <br/>Please keep shooting and entering,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Hmm...the dog looks more like a cat than a dog, and I have my doubts as to whether you could get this shot with a 500mm f.4 unless you''re about 10 feet tall, and even then you would still barely squeeze the head in.  Part of it, maybe.  The effects, added or in-camera, are a little distracting and it seems that you have some odd material for floors in Russia. Still, you got some love from the more seditious members here -  cutout and  posthumous like it, so it can''t be all bad.  Getting a Posty is a bit of a compliment so make sure you post it prominently on your user page! Please keep shooting and entering, Susan', '2016-01-27 18:30:05.000000', NULL, 0),
